### The `upper` field and renumbering (replace_children)

This is for incremental reparsing (U9), but it's relevant to understand how numberize is reused. The `upper` field stores `within.end` for an inner node — the upper bound of the numbering range. During renumbering (replace_children, node.rs:737-845), when children are replaced, it recomputes the `[start_number, end_number)` interval from the `upper` of the previous child and the number of the next child, then calls `numberize(span, id, Some(renumber), within)` to renumber just a subrange of children. If that fails (Unnumberable), it exponentially expands the range.

This is the "left half" trick paying off: because numberize left the right half empty, renumbering new children often succeeds without disturbing siblings.

